  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tMTD IT\n\t\tMTD IT\n\n### How to record Bank Interest for UK Property Using the Bridging Spreadsheet\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Thu, 6 Aug, 2026 at  3:39 PM\n\nWhen reporting UK Property income through the Capium MTD IT Bridging Spreadsheet, it is important to record Residential Financial Costs correctly to ensure that qualifying finance costs are reported in accordance with HMRC's Making Tax Digital for Income Tax (MTD IT) requirements.  \n\nResidential Financial Costs generally include finance costs incurred wholly or exclusively for a residential property rental business, such as: \n\nInterest on loans used to purchase or improve residential rental property.\nInterest in business overdrafts used exclusively for the property rental business.\n\nThese costs are reported separately because HMRC applies special tax relief rules for individual residential landlords. \n\nPlease do not include the following as Residential Financial Costs: \n\nPersonal loan interest \nSavings account interest received \nPersonal credit card interest \nProperty repairs and maintenance expenses \nMortgage capital repayments \n\nStep 1: Download the UK Property Bridging Spreadsheet \n\nBefore recording any Residential Financial Costs, download the UK Property Bridging Spreadsheet from the client's digital records. \n\nNavigation: MTD IT → Submissions → Select Client → UK Property Source → View & Submit \n\nNote: Capium provides separate Bridging Spreadsheet templates for: \n\nSole Trader \n\nUK Property \n\nForeign Property \n\nFor residential rental income and related finance costs, always use the UK Property template. \n\nOnce the template has been downloaded, you can begin entering your property transactions. \n\nStep 2: Record the information in the Template \n\nOpen the downloaded UK Property template and enter each qualifying finance cost as an individual transaction in the adjustment sheet of the template file. \nVerify that the information entered matches the supporting lender or bank statements before saving the spreadsheet.\n\nStep 3: Upload the Completed template file \n\nAfter entering all relevant transactions, Save the completed spreadsheet. \nReturn to the client's UK Property submission screen and upload the completed Spreadsheet using the upload option. \nNavigation:  Submission > Digital records > Click Drag & drop the file to upload the template file.\n\nStep 4: Review the Imported summary \n\nOnce the spreadsheet has been uploaded successfully \n\nNavigate to the Income & Expenses summary and review each category carefully to ensure all transactions have been categorized appropriately \n\nNavigation: MTD > Client specific source -UK property > View & Submit > Submissions > Summary of Each category  \n\nStep 5 : Submit the UK Property Update to HMRC \n\nAfter reviewing the imported data Confirm the Income & Expenses summary is correct and select the option Submit to HMRC at the bottom of the page. \n\n Related:\nClick here to find out more about Tax relief from HMRC \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
  "bodyHtml": "\n\t<div class=\"breadcrumb\">\n\t\t<a href=\"/support/solutions\"> Solution home </a>\n\t\t<a href=\"/support/solutions/9000118618\">MTD IT</a>\n\t\t<a href=\"/support/solutions/folders/9000201911\">MTD IT</a>\n\t</div>\n\t<b class=\"page-stamp page-stamp-article\">\n\t\t<b class=\"icon-page-article\"></b>\n\t</b>\n\n\t<h2 class=\"heading\">How to record Bank Interest for UK Property Using the Bridging Spreadsheet\n\t \t<a href=\"#\"\n            class=\"solution-print--icon print--remove\"\n \t\t\ttitle=\"Print this Article\"\n \t\t\tarial-role=\"link\"\n \t\t\tarial-label=\"Print this Article\"\n\t\t\tid=\"print-article\"\n \t\t>\n\t\t\t<span class=\"icon-print\"></span>\n\t\t\t<span class=\"text-print\">Print</span>\n \t\t</a>\n\t</h2>\n\t\n\t<p>Modified on: Thu, 6 Aug, 2026 at  3:39 PM</p>\n\t<hr />\n\t\n\n\t<article class=\"article-body\" id=\"article-body\" rel=\"image-enlarge\">\n\t\t<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">When reporting UK Property income through the Capium MTD IT Bridging Spreadsheet, it is important to record Residential Financial Costs correctly to ensure that qualifying finance costs are reported in accordance with HMRC's Making Tax Digital for Income Tax (MTD IT) requirements. &nbsp;</span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Residential Financial Costs generally include finance costs incurred wholly or exclusively for a residential property rental business, such as:&nbsp;</span></span